! Overview

''HyperGSD'' is a series of plugins that helps you <dfn>Get Stuff Done</dfn>, supported by a rich <dfn>Hypermedia</dfn> data model and associated tooling, all with the goal of helping you manage and prioritise the things you need to do.

HyperGSD uses technologies from the core of TiddlyWiki as much as possible. It is intended to integrate with an all-in-one personal TiddlyWiki and exist in the same wiki as your information, but you may also use it standalone. It is intended for use and tested with the the //Vanilla// theme.

; Actions (tasks)
: Short, ideally single-step actions that accomplish a task.<br>Actions may also carry dependencies to/from other actions.
; Projects
: A collection of Actions that have a similar purpose or goal.
; Realms
: Divide your Actions/Projects into appropriate, custom groupings by tagging with `"$:/GSD/Realm/<RealmName>` (e.g. <<tag-pill $:/GSD/Realm/Personal>>, <<tag-pill $:/GSD/Realm/Professional>>...)
; Dashboards
: Manage your actions and projects through a number of dashboards and views.

This wiki has several sub-plugins already installed providing more capabilities, like listing [[Contacts|$:/plugins/yan/hypergsd-contacts]] and setting [[Priorities|$:/plugins/yan/hypergsd-priorities]].

You can interact with these through the options available on the //Capture// and //Review// sidebar tabs, as well buttons on the Page Toolbar, like {{$:/plugins/yan/hypergsd/ui/sidebar/capture/new-action}}.

For background on how and why HyperGSD was created, see [[HyperGSD project background]].

! Install HyperGSD

Drag-and-drop the main ''HyperGSD plugin'' to your wiki to install:

<$let qualified-state=<<qualify "$:/state/plugin">> default-popup-state="yes">
{{$:/plugins/yan/hypergsd||$:/core/ui/Components/plugin-info}}
</$let>

If you are coming from GSD5, please also drag-and-drop to import the [[Migrating from GSD5 to HyperGSD]] tiddler and follow the instructions listed there.

